# Frontend (vanilla JS)

No frameworks — HTML/CSS/JS only. Match existing structure in `frontend/src/`.

## Files

- `index.html` — markup only
- `css/style.css` — design tokens, components
- `js/config.js` — `window.APP_CONFIG.apiBase` (`/api` in Docker, `http://localhost:8000` locally)
- `js/api.js` — shared `apiRequest()` with `credentials: 'include'`
- `js/auth.js`, `js/meal_plan.js`, `js/profile.js`, `js/utils.js` — feature modules

## API calls

- Docker: requests go to `/api/...` (nginx proxy).
- Local dev: `api.js` falls back to `http://localhost:8000` when placeholder not replaced.
- Always use `apiRequest()` — do not duplicate fetch logic.
- Session auth is cookie-based (`sf_session_id`); no manual token storage except display email in `localStorage`.

## UI conventions

- Auth overlay until logged in; main `#app` hidden until session valid.
- Check session on load via `GET /auth/me`.
- Use existing CSS variables and component classes — extend `style.css`, do not inline styles.
- Russian UI copy.

## New UI features

- Add DOM to `index.html`, styles to `style.css`, logic to the appropriate `js/` module.
- Handle loading/error states; reuse `showToast()` from `utils.js` when appropriate.
- If adding a new backend endpoint, backend tests are required (see `backend-testing.mdc`).
